# TestByIDOpsDoNotTargetRawWorkStores baseline (cmd/gc/byid_raw_store_guard_test.go).
#
# A row is file<TAB>function<TAB>rule<TAB>count: the number of sites in that
# function where a by-id bead op (rule byid), a front-door constructor
# (frontdoor), a class-handle relabel (relabel) or a package helper whose
# beads.Store parameter reaches one (via) is aimed at a RAW work or rig store.
# On a split city a coordination-class bead lives only in its relocated class
# binding, so such an op reads "not found" or patches a stale pre-migration copy.
#
# The counts may only fall. Growth fails, and so does a row the tree no longer
# reaches: lower or delete it in the change that retires the site.
#
# A NEW hit is fixed, not baselined: route the read through cliByIDOwner /
# classRoutedStoreForID / cliByIDBindingOwner or the class resolvers
# (cliSessionStore, cliStores(...).X(), resolve*Store). If the bead is
# work-class by construction, add a trailing `// byid:allow <reason>` on the
# flagged line (the line of the method selector, callee name or Store: key)
# instead; the reason is the review. A marker inside a helper does not exempt
# the helper's callers.
#
# UPDATE_BYID_RAW_STORE_GOLDEN=1 go test ./cmd/gc/ -run TestByIDOpsDoNotTargetRawWorkStores
# lowers or drops rows in place and files every new or grown key in an
# UNDOCUMENTED group, which the test refuses however often it is rerun: every
# row must sit under a "## <reason>" header.

## work-store base by construction: runBdStoreBridge is the bd-workspace bridge, and the gc bd close gate judges the bead bd itself is about to close in the store bd serves
cmd_bd_store_bridge.go	runBdStoreBridge	byid	9
cmd_bd_store_bridge.go	runBdStoreBridge	via	1
work_record_gate.go	runWorkRecordCloseGate	via	1

## hook claim seams wrapped by classRoutedHookClaimOps: each runs on the work-scope bd context first and escalates to the class binding on a not-found the route proves the binding holds (Claim, StampWorkMeta, ReadWorkMeta, AssignContinuation, Release, RestampAdopted, SkipDoneWorkflow, EmitExecutionStepStarted)
cmd_hook_claim.go	emitExecutionStepStarted	relabel	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookAssignContinuationWithBdStore	byid	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookClaimReleaseWithBdStore	byid	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookClaimRestampWithBdStore	byid	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookClaimWithBdStore	byid	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookReadClaimedBeadWithBdStore	byid	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookSkipDoneWorkflowWithBdStore	via	1
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookStampWorkMetaWithBdStore	byid	1

## KNOWN GAP (follow-up): the ConfirmBlocked seam is NOT wrapped by classRoutedHookClaimOps (cmd_hook_claim.go applyDefaults), so on a split city it reads a binding-resident bead's blocks deps on the work-scope bd context
cmd_hook_claim.go	hookConfirmBeadBlockedWithBdStore	via	1

## storage migration tools operate on pre-migration work copies by definition
infra_class_clear.go	clearRetainedInfraCopies	byid	2
infra_class_clear.go	clearRetainedInfraCopies	via	3
infra_class_migrate.go	runInfraClassMigrationFrom	via	3
infra_class_recover.go	doStorageRecoverStranded	via	2
storage_preflight.go	doStoragePreflight	via	1

## raw fallback of the bd on_close autoclose hooks: reached only when autocloseOwningStore resolves no owning store (an external checkout with no city.toml, or an unloadable config), it reads the just-closed bead on the cwd store bd serves; graph-class reads go through cliGraphStore, and the controller's beadCloseAutoclose covers binding rows
cmd_convoy.go	doConvoyAutoclose	via	1
molecule_autoclose.go	doMoleculeAutoclose	via	1
wisp_autoclose.go	doWispAutoclose	via	1

## pool-assigned work beads: releaseOrphanedPoolAssignments writes only work beads on their owner store; its one relabel (beads.SessionStore{Store: store}) is a nil-session-store fallback both callers make unreachable by passing a routed session store
city_runtime.go	CityRuntime.beadReconcileTick	via	1
cmd_start.go	doStartStandalone	via	1

## work-class by construction: GitHub PR repair beads are task beads in the rig's work store
cmd_github.go	ensureGitHubPRRepairBead	via	1

## control dispatch: the control bead's scope store is a work leg (or, from findBeadScopeAcrossStores, a relic leg or the binding); the gated bead is re-read from the store the dispatch mutates, and graph-class reads go through controlBeadLedger's separately routed graph store
cmd_convoy_dispatch.go	runControlDispatcher	via	1
cmd_convoy_dispatch.go	runControlDispatcherInStore	via	1

## relic legs (S4 debt): findBeadScopeAcrossStores probes the city and rig scope stores through beads.RelicGet, which counts each read as relic debt, before the graph binding leg
cmd_convoy_dispatch.go	findBeadScopeAcrossStores	via	2

## binding-first: the class binding is asked before the raw read (loadWaitDependencyBead through cliByIDBindingOwner; probeExistingSlingSourceBead through sling.ProbeBeadInStore on the binding); the guard cannot see the ordering
cmd_sling.go	probeExistingSlingSourceBead	via	1
cmd_wait.go	cmdSessionWait	via	1

## refused split shapes: newFormulaCookCmd's graph.v2 attach arm runs attachGraftClassRefusal and refuses when graphPlacementForScope differs from store; past those refusals placement == store, which holds because partial splits are refused at startup
cmd_formula.go	newFormulaCookCmd	byid	1
cmd_formula.go	newFormulaCookCmd	relabel	1
cmd_formula.go	newFormulaCookCmd	via	8

## relic-sweep legs: completionReconcileInputs leads with the routed graph store; it always sweeps the city work leg and each awake rig leg not yet proven relic-free, because pre-S4 graph.v2 roots may remain there; the runtime plane stops at the first (graph) leg
api_state.go	controllerState.completionReconcileInputs	relabel	1

## scope carrier: openOrderStoreForOrder labels the order's scope work store, and every consumer re-routes it through cliStores(...).Orders() (orderTrackingFrontDoor)
order_store.go	openOrderStoreForOrder	relabel	1

## KNOWN GAP (follow-up, SPLIT CAVEAT at the site): scopedStoreLike is class-blind; gc status's session snapshot stays on the routed store only because scopedStoreLike passes a non-bd-CLI store (every class binding today) through unchanged
cmd_citystatus.go	loadStatusSessionSnapshot	via	1
